<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were steady to lower on Friday, reflecting the soft rates in the overnight money market, traders said.</p>
<p>The one-week, two and three-month rates dipped after rising slightly on Thursday.</p>
<p>Dealers said banks continued to be swamped with pesos since they have been shying away from term reverse repos which have a 20 percent tax.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 21		 FEB 20</p>
<p>    1 W		9  7/8		  9 15/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/16		10  1/16</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/16		10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10  1/8		 10  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  5/16		10  5/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/2		 10  1/2</p>
<p>    VAL		24-Feb		  21-Feb</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
